title: "Agile forecasting's 85% delivery dates came true 80% of the time"
abstract: "In a pre-registered test on 25 public Apache Jira projects, the Monte Carlo forecasts behind many agile tools were too optimistic. Correcting each project's odds from its own track record brought its 85% statements back to about 85%, but did not make every probability more accurate. Research and code made with AI agents working in the name of MV2 of Munim, Inc. Code licensed Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0 unless a file says otherwise."
